[
    {
        "content": "<p>Currently, when the terminal is resized and the program is subscribed to the <code>WINCH</code> event, a resize cancels what the program is doing.</p>\n<p>Start a long running HTTP request, or a subprocess, and it gets canceled because the resize. All I want is to know the new size of the terminal, not to stop what the program is doing. Or not even know the size of the terminal, only that a resize happened, so the terminal will have to be checked some time later.</p>\n<p>In Zig or Crystal (and probably in Rust and Go and many other languages), it's approximately 3 minutes to write the necessary code by hand.<br>\nIn Roc, I gave up after an hour of discussing different possible workaround hacks with an LLM.</p>\n<p>This kind of friction is what causes most developers to pick another language.<br>\nIn Roc, hard tasks are easy, and trivial tasks are impossible.</p>",
        "id": 644369987,
        "sender_full_name": "notramo",
        "timestamp": 1795877165
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'll take a look</p>",
        "id": 644373691,
        "sender_full_name": "Anton",
        "timestamp": 1795879295
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I was thinking about a possible solution, that enables the necessary flexibility, similar to other languages while still preserving the Roc paradigms.</p>\n<p>The platform would require a <code>signal_handler!</code> function.</p>\n<p>When a signal comes in, don't do anything with the main thread yet. Run the <code>signal_handler!</code> on another thread.</p>\n<p><code>signal_handler!</code> returns a struct with two fields:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"roc\"><pre><span></span><code>SignalHandlerReturn := {\n    ## `CustomResult` is a user-specified type.\n    ## The content of this field is stored in the platform.\n    result: CustomResult,\n\n    ## `Interrupt` causes an `Interrupted` error on the main thread (current behavior).\n    ## `Continue` does not disturb the main thread.\n    action: [Interrupt, Continue]\n}\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The <code>CustomResult</code> is different in every app. In most apps it carries something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"roc\"><pre><span></span><code>CustomResult := {\n    event: [Resize(TerminalSize), Interrupt, Usr1]\n}\n\nTerminalSize := {\n    cols: U16,\n    lines: U16,\n}\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This can be used to run custom logic to decide what happens:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>There are multiple ways to query the terminal size: ANSI codes or an <code>ioctl</code> call.</li>\n<li>Some programs might want to complete the current rendering cycle before handling an interrupt event.</li>\n<li>Some programs need to cancel on certain signals, while simply queue the other signals, e.g. until the next render cycle.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Then <code>Signal.get_result!</code> can be used to access the <code>result</code> field in the struct returned by <code>signal_handler!</code>. Maybe repurpose <code>Signal.poll!</code>?</p>",
        "id": 644373700,
        "sender_full_name": "notramo",
        "timestamp": 1795879299
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The <code>TerminalSize</code> concept might actually work in the browser too.</p>",
        "id": 644373973,
        "sender_full_name": "Steve Howell",
        "timestamp": 1795879495
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>When a signal comes in, don't do anything with the main thread yet. Run the <code>signal_handler!</code> on another thread.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Here you would not have access to the app state right?</p>\n<p>We could do a <code>watch! : List(Request) =&gt; Try({}, [SignalErr(IOErr)])</code> which would allow you to register a specific event so it does not cancel anything. It would make <code>Stdin</code> reads and sleeps return <code>Interrupted</code> and on interrupt you can use <code>poll!</code> to check for the event, so:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"CoffeeScript\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nx\">Signal</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">watch</span><span class=\"o\">!</span><span class=\"p\">([</span><span class=\"nx\">WindowResize</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">unix</span><span class=\"p\">)])</span><span class=\"o\">?</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">Signal</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">catch</span><span class=\"o\">!</span><span class=\"p\">([</span><span class=\"nx\">Interrupt</span><span class=\"p\">])</span><span class=\"o\">?</span>\n\n<span class=\"nv\">response</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Http</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">send</span><span class=\"o\">!</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">request</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">?</span>\n\n<span class=\"nx\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Stdin</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">bytes</span><span class=\"o\">!</span><span class=\"p\">()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Ok</span><span class=\"nf\">(bytes) =&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">handle_input</span><span class=\"o\">!</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">bytes</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Err</span><span class=\"nf\">(Interrupted) =&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Signal</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">poll</span><span class=\"o\">!</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"nx\">contains</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">WindowResize</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"nx\">redraw</span><span class=\"o\">!</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"nx\">cleanup_and_exit</span><span class=\"o\">!</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Err</span><span class=\"nf\">(other) =&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Err</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">other</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>What do you think?</p>",
        "id": 644376666,
        "sender_full_name": "Anton",
        "timestamp": 1795881257
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It would be nice if there was some synergy here for browser apps, because it's often useful to have a browser alternative for native apps, and we solve similar problems. Treat this as would-be-nice request, not a blocker, for me. The API is from Claude:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"CoffeeScript\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nx\">roc</span>\n<span class=\"nx\">app</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">init</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">step</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">view</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">pf</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">platform</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"canvas\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">## What the screen is right now. A terminal host fills the same record</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">## in character cells; a canvas host in CSS pixels plus the pixel ratio.</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">Viewport</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">width</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">U32</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">height</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">U32</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">scale</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">F32</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">## Everything that happened since the last step, in order. Nothing interrupts.</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">Event</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Resize</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Viewport</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Key</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">key</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Str</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">down</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Bool</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">mods</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Mods</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Pointer</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">F32</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">F32</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">buttons</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">U8</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">phase</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">Down</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Move</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Up</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Wheel</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">dx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">F32</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">dy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">F32</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Focus</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Bool</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Visibility</span><span class=\"p\">([</span><span class=\"nx\">Shown</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Hidden</span><span class=\"p\">]),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Replied</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">U32</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">answer</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Reply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}),</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"c1\"># the answer to an earlier Request</span>\n<span class=\"p\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"nv\">Frame</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">now_ms</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">F64</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">dt_ms</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">F64</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">viewport</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Viewport</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">events</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">List</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Event</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">## Work the app wants done outside: it answers later as a Replied event.</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">Request</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Fetch</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">U32</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">url</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Str</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Store</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">key</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Str</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">bytes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">List</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U8</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Load</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">U32</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">key</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Str</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Sound</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">name</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Str</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nx\">Title</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Str</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"p\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"nv\">init</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Viewport</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Model</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">step</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Model</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Frame</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">model</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Model</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">requests</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">List</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Request</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">view</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Model</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Viewport</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">List</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Shape</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 644377593,
        "sender_full_name": "Steve Howell",
        "timestamp": 1795881905
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I feel like that API would shift basic-cli substantially towards a TUI platform and I'd rather have two different focused platforms in that case.</p>",
        "id": 644391845,
        "sender_full_name": "Anton",
        "timestamp": 1795891012
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think I lobbied for the removal of <code>enable_raw_mode!</code> from basic-cli many years ago for similar reasons.</p>",
